const slides = [{
    title: 'Blood donation project',
    description: 'When an individual contributes a blood donation, the National Health Service Blood and Transplant (NHSBT) promptly notifies them regarding the specific utilization of their donated blood, whether it is allocated to a hospital, employed for training purposes, or allocated elsewhere. However, the NHSBT mobile application currently lacks the provision of historical data concerning the ultimate destinations of previous donations. It is this deficiency that inspired the creation of the proposed application. This application aims to provide comprehensive historical information, visually represented on a map, illustrating the locations where each blood donation has been allocated, thereby facilitating the identification of clusters and offering a more convenient and intuitive overview of their final destinations. Through the accumulation of multiple donations, a visual graph is generated, elucidating the distribution pattern of an individual\'s donated blood and highlighting the regions with a higher probability of receiving their contributions compared to others.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'After careful consideration, I opted to develop the application as a progressive web application (PWA). This decision was motivated by several factors. Firstly, the application\'s lightweight nature aligns well with the capabilities of PWAs, which offer a seamless user experience across different devices and network conditions. Additionally, PWAs represent an emerging technology that has captured my keen interest, as I firmly believe it has the potential to significantly influence the landscape of web development in the near future. By embracing this technology, I not only aim to leverage its advantages for the current project but also view it as an opportunity for personal growth and learning, allowing me to expand my expertise in this evolving domain.',
    link: 'https://blood.martynrobotham.co.uk'
}];
